# Project: Gym SaaS (India-first, MVP)

Multi-surface product, one backend:
- S1 Mobile (React Native) — Client + Trainer core flows, light Admin
- S2 Web Admin (Next.js, App Router) — THIS REPO. Dashboards, renewals inbox,
  CRM pipeline, roster tables, desk attendance, plan catalog
- S3 API (Node/Express + Supabase/Postgres) — auth (email OTP), tenancy,
  jobs, push, food catalog, audit trail

## Non-negotiable domain rules
- Two account lanes: CLIENT and STAFF. A CLIENT can never become STAFF and
  vice versa. Never write code that lets a user switch lanes.
- Every gym is a tenant (GymOrg). Every query that touches gym-scoped data
  MUST be filtered by gym_org_id. There is no cross-tenant read, ever.
- Joins are invite-only. There are no open join codes. Do not build or
  suggest an open-code join flow (explicitly deferred, see docs/MVP_ROADMAP.md).
- Personal fitness/health data (progress, nutrition, wearables) is
  CLIENT-OWNED. Trainers/Admins can only read it if a DataGrant exists for
  that specific scope (PROGRESS, CALORIES, WEARABLES). No grant = no access,
  no exceptions, no "just for debugging."
- Roles: CLIENT, UNASSIGNED, TRAINER, ADMIN. A role code alone never unlocks
  data — every sensitive action must pass: auth -> role check -> tenant
  check -> grant check (see security-data-access.mdc).
- Billing is base + addons with price snapshots — never recompute historical
  invoices from current prices; always read the snapshot stored at
  purchase/renewal time.
- English UI only for this MVP. Do not add i18n scaffolding.

